<http://example.org/airkg/risk/atlas-data-provenance> <http://example.org/airkg#description> "Data provenance refers to the traceability of data (including synthetic data), which includes its ownership, origin, transformations, and generation. Proving that the data is the same as the original source with correct usage terms is difficult without standardized methods for verifying data sources or generation." .
<http://example.org/airkg/risk/atlas-data-provenance> <http://example.org/airkg#identifier> "atlas-data-provenance" .
<http://example.org/airkg/risk/atlas-data-provenance> <http://example.org/airkg#name> "Uncertain data provenance" .
