<http://example.org/airkg/risk/atlas-exploit-trust-mismatch-agentic> <http://example.org/airkg#description> "Attackers might initiate injection attacks to bypass the trust boundary, which is a distinct point or conceptual line where the level of trust in a system, application or network changes. Background execution in multi-agent environments increases the risk of covert channels if input/output validation is weak." .
<http://example.org/airkg/risk/atlas-exploit-trust-mismatch-agentic> <http://example.org/airkg#identifier> "atlas-exploit-trust-mismatch-agentic" .
<http://example.org/airkg/risk/atlas-exploit-trust-mismatch-agentic> <http://example.org/airkg#name> "Exploit trust mismatch" .
