<http://example.org/airkg/risk/atlas-membership-inference-attack> <http://example.org/airkg#description> "A membership inference attack repeatedly queries a model to determine if a given input was part of the model's training. More specifically, given a trained model and a data sample, an attacker appropriately samples the input space, observing outputs to deduce whether that sample was part of the model's training." .
